WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.807
NumPy includes several functions for creating numerical sequences without typing every value manually.

00:00:06.807 --> 00:00:13.372
The A-range function creates a sequence using a starting point, stopping point, and step.

00:00:13.372 --> 00:00:19.790
The lin space function creates a specific number of evenly spaced values between two endpoints.

00:00:20.489 --> 00:00:24.296
We can also create arrays filled with zeros or ones.

00:00:24.296 --> 00:00:30.816
These are useful when we want to initialize a structure before filling it with calculated values.

00:00:30.816 --> 00:00:39.616
In real projects, these functions are useful for simulations, building test data, defining ranges for plots,

00:00:39.616 --> 00:00:42.556
and preparing arrays with a known shape.

00:00:42.556 --> 00:00:47.539
Focus on the purpose of each function rather than memorizing the syntax.
